{"content": {"exact_text": "The scarcity of high-quality datasets in network intrusion detection presents significant challenges, especially in realworld applications. Existing datasets are often outdated or insufficient in both quality and quantity", "field": "traffic.dataset", "negative_state": null, "numeric": null}, "created_at": "2026-09-02T21:25:07.173378Z", "decisions": [], "evidence_type": "dataset_description", "id": "E0018", "origin": "author_claimed", "provenance": {"actor": "scripted/scripted-1", "note": null, "run_id": "run_20260902T212505Z_d6c8d3aa", "source": "model", "template_version": "1.0.0", "workflow": "interrogate"}, "qualification": null, "review_tier": 1, "schema_version": 1, "source": {"artifact": "A0005-1", "bbox": {"x0": 311.98, "x1": 563.04, "y0": 284.63, "y1": 557.78}, "block": "B0157", "char_end": 405, "char_start": 184, "file_hash": "sha256:24364d593c6b15646dc11838204bc9854d4982e2951c03004b0b8ccebe8ebd91", "page": 5, "section_path": ["COGNITIVE"], "text_hash": "sha256:466244524612aaa7493ff9ba1ab9605e74a1a84a10a60f571feb063b7cfd5bd3", "version": "V0005-1", "work": "W0005"}, "stale": "fresh", "strength": "direct", "updated_at": "2026-09-02T21:38:28.820731Z", "verification": {"accepted_by": "human", "extractor": "scripted/scripted-1", "rationale": "The span is the survey's own statement about the dataset landscape.", "review_action": "accept", "reviewed_at": "2026-09-02T21:38:28.820714Z", "status": "accepted", "verdict": "supported", "verifier": "scripted/scripted-1"}}
{"content": {"exact_text": "Meng et al. [1] developed NetGPT, which integrates multi-modal traffic modeling by encoding heterogeneous network traffic headers and payloads into a unified text input", "field": "traffic.representation_family", "negative_state": null, "numeric": null}, "created_at": "2026-09-02T21:25:07.074219Z", "decisions": [], "evidence_type": "method_description", "id": "E0028", "origin": "author_interpreted", "provenance": {"actor": "scripted/scripted-1", "note": null, "run_id": "run_20260902T212505Z_d6c8d3aa", "source": "model", "template_version": "1.0.0", "workflow": "interrogate"}, "qualification": null, "review_tier": 2, "schema_version": 1, "source": {"artifact": "A0005-1", "bbox": {"x0": 311.98, "x1": 563.04, "y0": 284.63, "y1": 557.78}, "block": "B0157", "char_end": 879, "char_start": 711, "file_hash": "sha256:24364d593c6b15646dc11838204bc9854d4982e2951c03004b0b8ccebe8ebd91", "page": 5, "section_path": ["COGNITIVE"], "text_hash": "sha256:466244524612aaa7493ff9ba1ab9605e74a1a84a10a60f571feb063b7cfd5bd3", "version": "V0005-1", "work": "W0005"}, "stale": "fresh", "strength": "indirect", "updated_at": "2026-09-02T21:39:27.620758Z", "verification": {"accepted_by": "human", "extractor": "scripted/scripted-1", "rationale": "The span describes a surveyed system's representation; strength indirect is appropriate.", "review_action": "accept", "reviewed_at": "2026-09-02T21:39:27.620739Z", "status": "accepted", "verdict": "supported", "verifier": "scripted/scripted-1"}}
{"content": {"exact_text": "LLMs may generate false positives due to biases in training data, struggle with inconsistent threat assessments, and even produce misleading outputs that could hinder security responses.", "field": "traffic.author_stated_limitations", "negative_state": null, "numeric": null}, "created_at": "2026-09-02T21:25:07.261298Z", "decisions": [], "evidence_type": "limitation", "id": "E0029", "origin": "author_claimed", "provenance": {"actor": "scripted/scripted-1", "note": null, "run_id": "run_20260902T212505Z_d6c8d3aa", "source": "model", "template_version": "1.0.0", "workflow": "interrogate"}, "qualification": null, "review_tier": 2, "schema_version": 1, "source": {"artifact": "A0005-1", "bbox": {"x0": 311.98, "x1": 563.04, "y0": 429.41, "y1": 606.75}, "block": "B0009", "char_end": 310, "char_start": 124, "file_hash": "sha256:24364d593c6b15646dc11838204bc9854d4982e2951c03004b0b8ccebe8ebd91", "page": 1, "section_path": ["Foundations, Implementations, and Future Directions"], "text_hash": "sha256:82e5e7450f0a41fb497d5d45606ac8c7cdef1ccdba33d53fa9c4b3ef70df7e9b", "version": "V0005-1", "work": "W0005"}, "stale": "fresh", "strength": "direct", "updated_at": "2026-09-02T21:39:32.841639Z", "verification": {"accepted_by": "human", "extractor": "scripted/scripted-1", "rationale": "The span states the limitation.", "review_action": "accept", "reviewed_at": "2026-09-02T21:39:32.841622Z", "status": "accepted", "verdict": "supported", "verifier": "scripted/scripted-1"}}
{"content": {"exact_text": "By leveraging LLMs, NIDS can transition from intelligent systems to cognitive systems capable of contextual reasoning, offering faster response and enhanced explainability.", "field": "traffic.llm_role", "negative_state": null, "numeric": null}, "created_at": "2026-09-02T21:25:07.131150Z", "decisions": [], "evidence_type": "method_description", "id": "E0037", "origin": "author_claimed", "provenance": {"actor": "scripted/scripted-1", "note": null, "run_id": "run_20260902T212505Z_d6c8d3aa", "source": "model", "template_version": "1.0.0", "workflow": "interrogate"}, "qualification": null, "review_tier": 1, "schema_version": 1, "source": {"artifact": "A0005-1", "bbox": {"x0": 311.98, "x1": 563.04, "y0": 175.09, "y1": 282.04}, "block": "B0005", "char_end": 512, "char_start": 340, "file_hash": "sha256:24364d593c6b15646dc11838204bc9854d4982e2951c03004b0b8ccebe8ebd91", "page": 1, "section_path": ["Foundations, Implementations, and Future Directions"], "text_hash": "sha256:f3903ed57f205ad3c6a4a5a1b2ad42bf7e301a5c8238f4ee5567e08b22d8da1a", "version": "V0005-1", "work": "W0005"}, "stale": "fresh", "strength": "direct", "updated_at": "2026-09-02T21:40:13.691019Z", "verification": {"accepted_by": "human", "extractor": "scripted/scripted-1", "rationale": "The span establishes the reasoning/explainer role.", "review_action": "accept", "reviewed_at": "2026-09-02T21:40:13.691001Z", "status": "accepted", "verdict": "supported", "verifier": "scripted/scripted-1"}}
